  "id": "formants",
  "term": "formants",
  "definition": "Formants are features of the vocal filtering system, commonly labeled F1 through F5, that help describe the acoustic structure of a voice during speech or singing. In this context, they are examined as part of how the vocal system is configured and may shift with emotion during performance.",
